{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Defiled.</b> In contrast to the first husband. Its reason: she is defiled to him because another man has known her. The dagesh in the tet is because of the absence of tav in the hitpa'el form. Likewise הכבד את הנגע." "<b>And you shall not cause to sin.</b> A command to Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Reading טעמו טמאה as 'its reason: she is defiled'; the manuscript has טמא' and בעבו' with suspensive abbreviations, resolved as טמאה and בעבור."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:36.627097989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}